<article class="env-definition" id="FE8042">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/FE8042">Definition <span data-tag="FE8042">6.1.1.2</span>.</a>colimit!universal Let $\calC $ be a presentable $\infty $-category. We will say that <em>colimits in $\calC $ are universal</em> if, for any morphism $f: T \rightarrow S$ in $\calC $, the associated pullback functor </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  f^{\ast }: \calC ^{/S} \rightarrow \calC ^{/T} \]
</div>
  <p> preserves (small) colimits. </p>
</article>